# {{PRODUCT}} Android agent instructions

Read `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`; it is the authoritative safety contract.

## Daily workflow

- Graph-backed discovery: exact code target -> task-context; feature/unknown/refactor -> harness graph; search never anchors discovery; search only in discovered scope.
- Do not inspect `.agents/scripts/**` during normal app work. Follow diagnostic boundary on failure.
- Clarify ambiguity before planning. When asked to explore edge cases or study scenarios before starting, present and discuss them in plain chat first. Approved plan required for mutations. Approval covers stated phases.
- Unified Chat & Question UI/UX (Language-Adaptive): Match the developer's active conversation language dynamically (never hardcode a fixed language) and use consistent Markdown layouts across every task (Plan Approval Card, Reviewer Dispatch Table `| Reviewer | Model | Status |`, Review Verdict Table `| Reviewer | Model | Verdict | Findings |`, 3-Section Mobile Walkthrough with `| # | Action | Expected Result |`, Commit Card with fenced Conventional Commit message, and structured `ask_question` modals). In any right-to-left (RTL) language, start every line/bullet with a word in that language and wrap every code symbol, file name, command, and English term in `` `backticks` ``.
- After approval, execute phases autonomously. Follow-ups within active scope must execute immediately: never generate redundant plan artifacts or stall for nonexistent UI buttons.
- Policy evaluates 6 risk tiers (`T0_TRIVIAL` to `T5_CRITICAL`) as runtime authority for gates, reviewers, and device. Execute the policy roster and always display each dispatched or completed reviewer alongside its active model from `reviewer_models` (`<role> [<model>]`) in chat.
- Query `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task status --task-id <id> --next` for canonical next actions.
- Verification order is preflight, tests, routed reviews, assemble/device, Mobile Verification Walkthrough and sign-off, then final verification.
- Never self-certify HIGH/CRITICAL reviews with `record_review.py --verdict PASS`. Adjudicate false positives via `validate-finding`. Never poll background work (Zero-Polling invariant).
- Context notes are administrative: clarify any ambiguity first, then structure, detail, and translate the developer's note into clear English before running `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py context note "<structured-english-note>"` (`--replace "<old>"` / `--remove "<old>"`). Always follow `.agents/project-context/project-notes.md` across all task phases and tracker mutations.

## Canonical Command Catalog

| Step | Command |
|---|---|
| Task context | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task-context --file <path> --json` |
| Feature / find graph | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py graph --feature <name> --json` |
| Task status | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task status --task-id <id> --next` |
| Context note | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py context note "<structured-english-note>"` (`--replace "<old>"` / `--remove "<old>"`) |
| Preflight | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py preflight` |
| Unit tests | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py test` |
| Review evidence | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/record_review.py --task <id> --response <role>=<unchanged-response-file>` |
| Resume | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task resume --task-id <id>` |
| Assemble | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` |
| Device | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device install-start` |
| Verify | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py verify --task-id <id>` |

